        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Maclaurin Expansion of a Logarithmic Function",
        "problem": "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2}).$",
        "worked_solution": "The Maclaurin series for $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)=x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $3{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2}) & =(3{x}^{2})-\\frac{1}{2}{(3{x}^{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{(3{x}^{2})}^{3}-⋯ \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}\\,{x}^{4}+9{x}^{6}-⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
